# Trivy suppressions for the CRITICAL gate in .github/workflows/build.yml.
#
# CRITICAL findings fail the build. HIGH and below are reported by the
# informational pass but never gate. Only add an entry here when the finding is
# genuinely not actionable in this repository — a vendored dependency inside a
# prebuilt upstream binary we do not compile. Every entry needs a reason, a
# date, and the condition under which it should be removed.
#
# Review these whenever a build's informational pass changes, and drop entries
# as soon as the upstream package is rebuilt.

# CVE-2026-33186 — google.golang.org/grpc v1.72.2, fixed upstream in 1.79.3.
# Vendored into a Go binary shipped by an upstream package (the image's Go
# binaries are tailscale/tailscaled, uupd and umotd; Trivy reports this against
# a content-addressed ostree object, so the exact one is unattributed). We do
# not build any of them, so the fix has to come from an upstream rebuild
# against newer grpc — there is no change we can make here.
# Added 2026-07-31. Remove once the upstream package ships grpc >= 1.79.3.
CVE-2026-33186
